sequenceDiagram
    participant E as Edge Management System
    participant K as Kafka-Compatible Data Distribution Service
    participant U as Authorized Logical Consumer A
    participant V as Authorized Logical Consumer B

    Note over K,V: Both consumers are authorized for the same configured target/topic
    E->>K: Publish GEISA data record 1 (Kafka Produce)
    K-->>U: Return record 1 when available
    K-->>V: Return record 1 when available
    U->>K: Commit Consumer A position
    V->>K: Commit Consumer B position

    Note over U,U: Consumer A becomes unavailable
    E->>K: Publish records 2 and 3
    K-->>V: Return records 2 and 3 when available
    V->>K: Commit Consumer B position
    Note over K,U: Records remain available according to configured retention

    Note over U,K: Consumer A reconnects
    U->>K: Resume continuous consumption from committed position
    K-->>U: Return retained records 2 and 3
    U->>K: Commit Consumer A position

    Note over U,V: One consumer's outage doesn't interrupt others consumption
